y cyclical work.'\nn='with four quoted bullets: superslow, active stretching, connective tissue first (Chapter 1 gives the basis and Chapter 6 the rule, both linked), low-intensity cyclical work.'\nassert t.count(o)==1; open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(t.replace(o,n)); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Note the wording polish in the fix log"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffrZXeMea3eDuGY43735","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e2f48b8a-987f-40a8-86c9-0f12d5353a89","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:28:00.323Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"e2f48b8a-987f-40a8-86c9-0f12d5353a89","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"189515d2-55e8-482a-8b52-f518760b72bc","agentId":"a738c543bcd777bcb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXXpduo8DugFjoLMCFN5Af","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4fb4e342-ea8c-404e-b103-3f06bf86e157","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:28:00.589Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch7a_applied.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":7,"newStart":13,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | framework--hybrid-repetitions-and-hybrid-sets.md | **Fix 5.** The \"Unclear as printed ... may be a set count\" note is replaced: \"By the 6.6.2 convention (PDF pp. 335-336 / printed pp. 324-325, checked against the page images, where \"60 x 10, 70 x 8, 80 x 6, 80 x 6\" is also written \"10(60)¹, 8(70)¹, 6(80)²\", so \"6(80)²\" means two sets of 6 at 80 kg) the superscript is the number of sets, so 80³ over 3+5+2 means three sets of the 10-repetition hybrid; the text's \"for a set of 3 repetitions\" conflicts with its own convention.\" When to apply now opens with the authors' use, \"When a circuit is to be condensed into one station (the authors' use, PDF p. 410)\", and the time/space clause follows as \"Inference: also when ...\". The Example now says \"written 80³ (three sets by the 6.6.2 convention)\". `untested` kept. |"," | heuristic--progressive-and-random-segmental-training.md | **Fix 6.** \"The random variant when a long block of one exercise has stalled\" is now \"The random variant from the start of a block, to limit early accommodation (the authors' stated purpose, PDF p. 410)\" (PDF 410 image: \"to minimise the possibility of early accommodation to a predictable regime\"). `untested` kept. |"," | framework--contrast-methods-load-release-pneumatics-heavy-light-set.md | **Fix 7.** (1) \"Why `contested`\" now opens \"The rating applies to the heavy-light set.\" \"The heavy-light set and load release rest on ...\" is now \"The heavy-light set rests on exactly the effect these studies disagree about\", followed by \"Load release and pneumatics unload within a single repetition; the cited studies did not test that, so the conflict does not reach them directly.\" (2) The Russian findings on PDF 175 are quoted verbatim with their citation lists: \"Dynamic work with heavy weights (i.e. high tension with relatively few repetitions) also elicits a positive after-effect in the central nervous system (CNS), which produces a general toning influence on the motor apparatus and an improvement in speed and strength (Portnov, 1955; Ratov, 1957; Diachkov, 1961; Muravov & Tkachev, 1964; Letunov, 1965)\" and \"intense preliminary strength tension improves results in jumping exercises (Diachkov, 1958; 1961; Verkhoshansky, 1961; Tatian, 1964; Tkachev, 1967), in shotputting (Fritsch, 1961; Ivanova, 1964; Markov, 1966), and in rowing (Ermishkin & Vozniak, 1965; Chuprun, 1966)\". When NOT now reads \"Do not expect a reliable acute boost from the heavy-light set: the Western studies the book cites are split (two found a faster unloaded movement, others found none), and the Russian studies it cites found one (PDF p. 175).\" `contested` kept. |","-| framework--strength-training-aims-and-method-chart-figs-7-1-and-7-2.md | **Missing ideas 1-5** (GO entry). New paragraph \"Sources and scope of the catalogue\": the five sources (PDF 404), \"Only in recent years, has science begun to investigate seriously ...\" (PDF 404), and the concluding \"rapid reference for the major methods which are most frequently used in the training of high-level athletes\" plus the magazine-methods exclusion (PDF 414), with \"Inference: most of the 7.1 catalogue rests on practice in the strength sports, not on studies cited on these pages.\" New block \"Notes beside Fig 7.1\" (PDF 405) with four quoted bullets: superslow, active stretching, connective tissue first, low-intensity cyclical work. When NOT adds \"Do not read the catalogue as tested: the authors say science has only \"in recent years\" begun to examine Iron Game practice (PDF p. 404).\" Related adds five links (below). `untested` kept. |","+| framework--strength-training-aims-and-method-chart-figs-7-1-and-7-2.md | **Missing ideas 1-5** (GO entry). New paragraph \"Sources and scope of the catalogue\": the five sources (PDF 404), \"Only in recent years, has science begun to investigate seriously ...\" (PDF 404), and the concluding \"rapid reference for the major methods which are most frequently used in the training of high-level athletes\" plus the magazine-methods exclusion (PDF 414), with \"Inference: most of the 7.1 catalogue rests on practice in the strength sports, not on studies cited on these pages.\" New block \"Notes beside Fig 7.1\" (PDF 405) with four quoted bullets: superslow, active stretching, connective tissue first (Chapter 1 gives the basis and Chapter 6 the rule, both linked), low-intensity cyclical work. When NOT adds \"Do not read the catalogue as tested: the authors say science has only \"in recent years\" begun to examine Iron Game practice (PDF p. 404).\" Related adds five links (below). `untested` kept. |"," "," ## Confidence rule, all 10 entries"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch7a_applied.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2f48b8a-987f-40a8-86c9-0f12d5353a89","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
